====================================================================================================
  READOUT AND GRADIENT UNDER EACH CONVENTION
====================================================================================================
  num_ancillas=3, margin=2.0, shots=4096, R=0.6, block 0,
  seeds 0-4. 'E err' is |E_qpe - E_exact| at the centre; 'cos' is the
  cosine between the block's sensed gradient and the exact gradient.

       problem   E err V3   E err V5    cos V3    cos V5    winner
  ----------------------------------------------------------------
      Heis N=4     0.1828     0.2386    0.9744    0.9587        V3
      Heis N=6     0.2386     0.1983    0.8770    0.7740        V3
    MaxCut N=4     0.2265     0.2265    0.9850    0.9850       tie
    MaxCut N=6     0.1597     0.2996    0.9584    0.7389        V3
      TFIM N=4     0.3907     0.2481    0.9670    0.9626       tie
            H2     0.0392     0.0445    0.9931    0.9730        V3

  If V3 wins on E err and cos with no aliasing flagged, V5 line 237 is a
  resolution regression and should read H0_norm. If they tie, the choice is
  free and V5's is the safer default. Either way the two files should stop
  disagreeing silently.
